>> title: New England Clam Chowder
>> category: Soups
>> tags: clams, potatoes, cream, seafood, stovetop
>> counters: Diner, One Pot
>> aka: clam chowder, white clam chowder, chowdah, cup of chowder
>> servings: 6
>> time: 50 min
>> slack: unforgiving — the last step is warmed through and never boiled, because a boiled chowder splits and the clams go to rubber, and neither comes back; clams are also a same-day ingredient, so this is not a chowder to leave on the stove all afternoon
>> step.1: render in a Dutch oven
>> step.2: sweat 8 min
>> step.3: stir in flour 2 min
>> step.4: simmer 15 min
>> step.5: warm through, no boil
>> step.6: season

Render @salt pork{3%oz}(85 g; diced, or bacon) in a #Dutch oven{} until crisp.

Sweat @&(~1)pork{} for ~{8%min} with @yellow onion{1%large}, @celery{2%ribs}, and @thyme{2%sprigs}.

Cook @&(~1)base{} for ~{2%min} with @all-purpose flour{3%Tbs}(25 g).

Simmer @&(~1)base{} for ~{15%min} with @Yukon Gold potatoes{1 1/2%lb}(700 g; cubed), @clam juice{3%cups}(720 mL), and @bay leaf{1}.

Warm @&(~1)chowder{} through without boiling with @chopped clams{2%cups}(with their liquor) and @heavy cream{1%cup}(240 mL).

Season @&(~1)chowder{} with @kosher salt{1%tsp} and @black pepper{1/2%tsp}.
